<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed weaker at -1.27 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed weaker at -1.27 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.4630 to the dollar, up from 3.4715 on Wednesday and at 1.8905 to the mark, down from 1.8830, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of -1.27 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, weaker than Wednesday's -1.23 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
